cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Stability, Consistency and Convergence of Linear Multistep Methods
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying report, please cite it."
type: software
# Two of the three authors appear only by initials in the report and slides
# (\author{L. T. Nhân \and D. T. H. Yến \and N. H. Tú}); they are recorded here
# exactly as the documents give them rather than expanded by guesswork.
authors:
  - family-names: L.
    given-names: T. Nhân
  - family-names: D.
    given-names: T. H. Yến
  - family-names: Nguyễn
    given-names: Hoàng Tú
abstract: >-
  A tested implementation and report on linear multistep methods for initial
  value problems: Adams-Bashforth, Adams-Moulton and BDF families with their
  coefficients derived rather than tabulated, root-condition and order checks,
  and a convergence study demonstrating the Dahlquist equivalence theorem —
  that consistency plus zero-stability gives convergence, and that dropping
  either one loses it.
keywords:
  - numerical analysis
  - ordinary differential equations
  - linear multistep methods
  - zero-stability
  - Dahlquist equivalence theorem
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2025-01-01"
